"""
Single source of truth for the curated incident database.

Conventions
-----------
* Amounts: *_usd_m are USD millions at (approximately) the exchange rate on the
  incident date as reported by the cited source. Original-currency strings are
  kept separately in *_orig. None = not publicly disclosed / unknown.
* status: CONFIRMED | REPORTED | ALLEGED | DISPUTED | INFERRED | UNKNOWN
  (refers to the headline facts of the record; per-field caveats in notes).
* evidence: 1 (single weak/secondary source) .. 5 (court record / regulator
  finding / audited disclosure plus independent corroboration).
* verification: "web-verified 2026-11-07" = content checked via live web search
  during this project; "canonical (training knowledge)" = well-documented
  historical fact recorded from the research team's prior knowledge with a
  canonical primary-source URL; the URL itself was NOT re-fetched this session.
* is_cyberattack: False for non-malicious comparators (kept for contrast).
* state_link: "confirmed-gov" (government attribution/indictment) |
  "suspected" (vendor/media attribution only) | "none-known" | "claimed"
  (self-claimed by a group, unverified).
"""

D = "Not publicly disclosed"

